### What pa3ds says in words of its own that only Omega Ruby and Alpha Sapphire have reason to:
### soaring, and what is on their maps alone. Read before every game's `words.ftl`.

## Soaring on Latios or Latias (spike 166)

# The sky's categories, the game's own grouping of its map's places by colour.
category-towns = towns
category-routes = routes
category-landmarks = landmarks
category-mirage-spots = mirage spots
# A flock of Pokémon flying over Hoenn, which the player flies into to battle one: the game draws
# the birds and never names them.
kind-flock = flock
# How far above or below the player a flock flies: "12 ahead, 2 below".
way-above = above
way-below = below
# Which way to turn to face a place or a flock: "turn left 40 degrees, 33 ahead".
sky-turn = turn { $way } { $degrees } degrees
# The way the player faces, as a turn stops on another: "facing north-east".
sky-facing = facing { $way }

## What is on ORAS's maps alone

kind-berry-spot = berry spot
kind-ash-pile = ash pile
kind-hidden-Pokemon = hidden Pokémon
kind-secret-base-spot = secret base spot
kind-ladder-up = ladder up
kind-ladder-down = ladder down
# Mossdeep Gym's (spike 163), Mauville Gym's (spike 146) and Dewford Gym's (spike 132).
kind-switch = switch
kind-conveyor-belt = conveyor belt
kind-lift = lift
# Lavaridge Gym's (spike 157).
kind-trapdoor = trapdoor
kind-geyser = geyser
